#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""verity-ask - the Verity OS AI helper (v0.2). No API key needed.

It answers using, in this order:
  1. local AI    a small open model running on YOUR PC (via Ollama)
                 set it up once:  verity ask --install-ai
  2. cloud AI    Claude, only if you saved an API key:  verity ask --setup
  3. built-in    an offline knowledge base - instant, always available

Usage:
  verity ask "how do I connect to wifi?"     one question
  verity ask                                 interactive chat
  some-command 2>&1 | verity ask "why?"      explain piped output
  verity ask --install-ai                    install the local AI (free, private)
  verity ask --status                        show which helpers are available
  verity ask --setup                         (optional) save a cloud API key
  verity ask --offline | --local | --cloud   force one helper
  verity ask --show-context                  show the system info that is shared
  verity ask --no-run                        never offer to run commands

Nothing is ever run without asking you first.
"""
